MRA REBUILD PROMPT — Consolidate 5-location emails into one daily digest
(v2 — updated after confirming template scales from 1 to N locations)

CONTEXT:
MRA currently generates and sends one separate 24-Hour Review Summary email
per client_id, each pulling from ALA, SIA, and RDA independently and firing
its own send. Aji Ceviche Bar (5 locations) receives 5 separate emails daily
for what is operationally one account.

UPDATE FROM PRIOR VERSION:
The consolidated HTML template has now been proven to scale cleanly at 1
location (PAK-001), 2 locations (EDO Restaurants), and 5 locations (Aji
Ceviche) using the exact same structure — header, aggregate strip, per-
location rows, footer. No separate "single-location" template is needed.
This resolves the open question from the prior version: MRA should build
ONE rendering path for all accounts, not two templates running in parallel.

RECOMMENDATION: Migrate PAK-001 and EDO-001 onto this same consolidated
template now, at the same time as the Aji Ceviche build — not after separate
validation. Reasoning: maintaining two templates (old single-location format
+ new consolidated format) is more ongoing MRA logic than migrating once.
The aggregate strip is harmless at 1 location (totals just equal that one
location's numbers) and harmless at 2 (already confirmed in the EDO mockup).
Miguel should confirm this recommendation before build starts.

OBJECTIVE:
Change MRA's email-generation logic from "one run per location_id → one
send per location_id" to "one run across all location_ids under a parent
account → one consolidated send," for ALL accounts (PAK-001, EDO-001,
AJI-001 through AJI-005), using a single template that scales by row count.

REQUIRED CHANGES TO MRA WORKFLOW:

1. ACCOUNT GROUPING
   - Client Config table needs a parent_account_id field linking every
     client_id to its parent account, even accounts with only one location
     (PAK-001 becomes its own single-row parent account; Aji Ceviche's 5
     locations share one parent account).
   - MRA's trigger runs once per parent_account_id, fetching the full list
     of child location_ids belonging to that account before proceeding.

2. PER-LOCATION DATA FETCH (loop, not separate runs)
   - For each location_id under the account: review_count, avg_rating,
     drafts_generated, drafts_generated_tier, signal_direction (%),
     top_domain, pending_approval_count — written to an array keyed by
     location_id, not sent immediately.

3. AGGREGATION STEP
   - After all locations are fetched, MRA computes account-level totals:
     total_reviews_24h, blended_avg_rating (weighted by review count),
     total_drafts_generated_24h, total_pending_all_locations.
   - At 1 location, these totals simply equal that location's own numbers —
     no special-case logic needed.
   - OPEN QUESTION (unresolved): confirm whether "pending" aggregates
     cumulative all-time pending or 24hr delta — changes the formula.

4. TOKEN GENERATION (per location, not per email)
   - One magic-link token per location_id, same as today. All tokens for
     an account are collected and passed into the single template as href
     values for each location's "View & Approve" button. At 1 location,
     this becomes a single full-width CTA button instead of a per-row
     button — template already supports both layouts.

5. SINGLE TEMPLATE RENDER
   - One render path handles 1, 2, or 5+ locations. Row count is the only
     variable — header, aggregate strip, footer stay identical.
   - Status stripe color per row: green if signal_direction ≥ majority
     positive, amber if mixed, red if majority negative.

6. SINGLE SEND
   - MRA fires exactly one email per parent_account_id per day, to the
     account's designated recipient(s).

